<title>USA: Electric Boat, Newport News still in talks.</title>
<headline>Electric Boat, Newport News still in talks.</headline>
<dateline>GROTON, Conn. 1997-01-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Electric Boat Co. said Friday it welcomed news that the Pentagon wants Congress to buy four submarines between 1998 and 2002, but said joint-venture talks with Newport News Shipbuilding were still preliminary.</p>
<p>&quot;What we've learned from the Thursday meeting (between top military officials and Connecticut and Virginia legislators) puts the conditions in place for the teaming effort to move forward,&quot; Electric Boat spokesman Neil Ruenzel told Reuters.</p>
<p>&quot;But many details need to be worked out between the shipyards and the Navy before the plan can become a reality.&quot;</p>
<p>Ruenzel did not elaborate.</p>
<p>Electric Boat is a subsidiary of General Dynamics.</p>
<p>--Hartford newsroom (860) 727-8608</p>
</text>
